 "notes": [
  "Values are copied from manufacturer or distributor datasheets; every item carries its source URL. Re-check against the datasheet before a purchase decision.",
  "dims: width x depth x height of the indoor unit as installed (for wall units, depth is the projection from the wall).",
  "cooling_total_w is the rated (nominal) cooling capacity at the manufacturer's standard conditions (typically 27 °C DB / 19 °C WB indoor, 35 °C outdoor) unless 'conditions' says otherwise.",
  "cooling_sensible_w is published only by Daikin here. For units without it, the calculation uses cooling_total_w x the room's sensible heat ratio setting and marks the result as estimated. Daikin's own figures below give a ratio of 0.66-0.73 for comfort units, so 0.7 is a reasonable default.",
  "power_input_w: rated electrical input in cooling at the same conditions (indoor + outdoor). 'derived' means computed from capacity / EER.",
  "airflow_m3h: indoor fan steps, highest first. The highest step is used for airflow checks.",
  "Comfort units (split_wall, ducted) are not designed as server room units: their sensible share is about 70 % and they are built for comfort duty. Precision units (in_row, precision_perimeter) are: sensible share close to 100 %, 24/7 duty, airflow sized for IT load. The rules engine flags comfort units cooling IT load (SPEC 12.3).",
  "Precision units are rated at their own test conditions (return air temperature and humidity in 'conditions'); these are hotter than comfort ratings, which is normal for server rooms."
 ],
